{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0170062","isObsolete":false,"name":"nutrient storage","definition":{"text":"The accumulation and maintenance in cells or tissues of a nutrient, a substance that is used by an organism to survive, to grow, and to reproduce; such as proteins, vitamins, and minerals. Nutrient reserves can be accumulated for mobilization and utilization when needed."},"children":[{"id":"GO:0019915","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0052576","relation":"is_a"},{"id":"GO:0140089","relation":"is_a"}],"history":[{"timestamp":"2025-01-31","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A substance that is used by an organism to survive, to grow, and to reproduce; such as proteins, vitamins, and minerals."},{"timestamp":"2025-01-31","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"The accumulation and maintenance in cells or tissues of a nutrient, a substance that is used by an organism to survive, to grow, and to reproduce; such as proteins, vitamins, and minerals. Nutrient reserves can be accumulated for mobilization and utilization when needed."},{"timestamp":"2024-12-03","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A substance that is used by an organism to survive, to grow, and to reproduce; such as proteins, vitamins, and minerals."},{"timestamp":"2024-12-03","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"nutrient storage"},{"timestamp":"2024-12-03","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0009987 (cellular process)"}],"aspect":"biological_process","usage":"Unrestricted"}],"pageInfo":null}